schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Decentralized Finance (DeFi)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Financial services (swaps, lending, stablecoins) built on public
    blockchains that operate without traditional intermediaries like banks;
    anyone with a wallet can access them directly.
  source_traditions:
    - Ethereum smart-contract protocol design (Uniswap, Aave, Compound, MakerDAO)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Introduced in this article as one of four pillars of the Ethereum
    ecosystem (alongside Layer 2s, NFTs, and DAOs), framed for regenerative
    communities as a lens on "community-controlled finance" running on
    transparent, auditable code rather than closed corporate infrastructure.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - Traditional finance (TradFi) intermediated by banks/brokers
    - Community currencies / local exchange systems (non-blockchain analogues)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      DeFi is permissionless access to financial primitives (swap, lend,
      borrow), not a guarantee of safety or fairness — it removes an
      intermediary, it does not remove risk.
  tensions:
    - >-
      The article's own caution ("smart contracts can have bugs... the space
      has seen significant losses from hacks and fraud") sits alongside its
      framing of DeFi as an opportunity for community finance; the two need to
      be held together, not resolved into pure optimism.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Presenting DeFi purely as "transparent, auditable" risks understating that
    audits are imperfect and that transparency does not equal safety for a
    first-time, low-resource user.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/ethereum-ecosystem.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
